[paste outerHTML]

Extend the previous script to scrape every page starting at https://books.toscrape.com/catalogue/page-1.html.
Page structure: each book is article.product_pod; the title is the title attribute of h3 a; the price is p.price_color; the rating is the second class of p.star-rating (One to Five). The next link is li.next a and is relative.
Requirements:
- paginate by following the next link, joining URLs with urljoin;
- set resp.encoding = "utf-8" and turn prices into numbers;
- time.sleep(1) between pages;
- save books.csv with pandas using utf-8-sig;
- finally print the average price per rating.

Refactor my scraper below so it is more robust and more polite:
- use requests.Session with User-Agent "LearningBot/0.1 (contact: my email)";
- retry 429 and 5xx responses 3 times with exponential backoff;
- check robots.txt with urllib.robotparser before fetching;
- log every URL and status code with logging;
- write finished URLs to done.txt and skip them on the next run.
Do not fake browser headers, and do not add anything that bypasses CAPTCHAs or blocks.

[paste your stage 3 code]

